_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-13T20:40:54Z","updated_at":"2022-04-13T20:41:08Z","body":"This looks, as if the check for version 8 is somehow returning that this is indeed a version 8 running. This check seems to return the version is version 8...\r\n\r\n```\r\nnew ComparableVersion(dockerImageName.getVersionPart()).isGreaterThanOrEqualTo(\"8.0.0\");\r\n```\r\n\r\n@brentryan can you share some code how you are initializing the container and what version you are using?\r\n\r\nThe following snippet worked for me, but maybe there is more to it:\r\n\r\n```\r\n        try (ElasticsearchContainer container = new ElasticsearchContainer(DockerImageName.parse(\"docker.elastic.co/elasticsearch/elasticsearch\").withTag(\"7.4.2\"))) {\r\n            // Start the container. This step might take some time...\r\n            container.start();\r\n        }\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/testcontainers/testcontainers-java/issues/comments/1098467030/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"spinscale","id":667544,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzU0NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/667544?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale","html_url":"https://github.com/spinscale","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/spinscale/gis